# Design mockups and data contracts — deliberately NOT published (2026-07-31).
#
# This repository is PUBLIC while the project's own posture is inner-source-first
# (CLAUDE.md, "Path C"). The sensitive tree is data-contracts/: it carries a
# Databricks workspace id, the org's real catalog/schema/table/column names with
# row counts, and UC column comments that name the org outright ("Denominator
# for FR PepsiCo") — 46 occurrences in one metric-view contract alone.
#
# It holds ZERO real data values — the privacy attestation in its MANIFEST was
# checked and holds (categorical values withheld, masked character-class
# patterns only, synthetic-generation rules). Schema TOPOLOGY plus the org's
# name on a public repo is still an org decision, and the decision was no.
#
# The Design/ extracts were checked too and carry no company references; they
# are ignored alongside because they are working inputs, not deliverables, and
# an owner decision covered both. (The Design/audit-findings files that were
# ALREADY tracked before this date stay tracked — git history keeps them
# regardless, and they are clean.)
#
# Everything stays on disk and stays usable — Design/unified-extract is the
# reference the design work is matched against. Ignoring keeps it off the
# internet and out of `git status` noise. Revisit if the repo goes private.
Design/
data-contracts/
data-contracts.zip
